libc++ (LLVM 18) <functional>: std::function<int(int)> holding a lambda
returns a nondeterministic value, so the first assertion fails.  The
remaining drops are tuple:469 __tuple_impl's constructor and
function.h:272: in `__tuple_leaf<_Uf, _Tf>(std::forward<_Up>(__u))...'
the call std::forward<_Up>(__u) does not resolve ("template 'forward' not
found"), so no __tuple_leaf constructor matches (being reduced:
/tmp/r163/red/kb_W_func_fwd; the earlier reduction kb_V_func_c lost
__tuple_leaf's constructors and showed a C++20 parenthesized aggregate
initialization gap instead, fixed: cpp20_parenthesized_aggregate_init_one_
element, cpp20_aggregate_element_of_class_type_constructed).  Type
checking takes about 2 minutes and the SAT solver needs more than 16 GB
(with `ulimit -v 16000000' the result is ERROR).  clang++ 18
-stdlib=libc++ accepts this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
